  "nl": "What places to visit in Bilbao",
  "trajectory_steps": [
   "user (None, score=None): What places to visit in Bilbao",
   "model (gpt-4, score=57): You should definitely visit the Guggenheim Museum for impressive modern and contemporary art. Consider exploring the Old Town (Casco Viejo), the heart of Bilbao with charming narrow streets. Other must-see sites include the Plaza Nueva, La Ribera Market, and the unique transport system - the Vizcaya Bridge.",
   "model (claude-2, score=69): Bilbao offers many great places to visit. The Guggenheim Museum with its iconic architecture is a must-see. Casco Viejo, the atmospheric old town, has charming streets to wander. Mount Artxanda provides lovely views over the city. The Mercado de la Ribera market is lively and full of delicious food. I'd also recommend seeing the Zubizuri Bridge and taking a walk along the Nervion River. Bilbao has an exciting mix of culture, architecture, and natural beauty to explore.",
   "model (claude-instant-1, score=55): The top attractions in Bilbao include the Guggenheim Museum, a landmark building and art gallery known for its impressive architecture and collection. Also popular is the Casco Viejo neighborhood, filled with charming streets, plazas and buildings dating back centuries. For beautiful scenery, take a stroll along the Nervión River promenade or visit Mount Pagasarri for panoramic city views. Food lovers enjoy exploring the many tapas bars and restaurants serving fresh seafood and Basque cuisine. Bilbao also has several parks like Doña Casilda Iturrizar Park for relaxing outdoors.",
   "model (timdettmers/guanaco-33b-merged, score=84): Bilbao is a city full of culture and history, and there are many places worth visiting. Here are a few of the most popular:\n\n1. The Guggenheim Museum Bilbao: This museum is an architectural masterpiece in itself, and it houses one of the finest collections of modern and contemporary art in the world.\n\n2. The Old Town: The Casco Viejo, or the Old Town, is the heart of Bilbao and is a must-visit for anyone who wants to get a sense of the city's history and culture. It is home to the Catedral de Santiago, the Mercado de la Ribera, and the Plaza Nueva.\n\n3. Mount Artxanda: For a panoramic view of the city, you can take a funicular ride to the top of Mount Artxanda. From here, you can see the whole city spread out before you",
