ted where a specific construct's grammar restricts which atom/value kinds it accepts (e.g. CONDITIONAL, ITERATION's collection). Any identifier appearing in expr/bool_expr/collection position must be a TASK parameter, a name bound via `->` earlier in the same scope, or an enclosing loop variable; any other bare identifier is an undefined-reference static error — external world resources, recipients, or objects that were never explicitly bound must be written as string_literal (e.g. `email(\"mom\")`, not `email(mom)`). expr deliberately excludes calls (no nested ACTION/CHECK/task_call inside an argument expression): to pass a prior step's result as a later argument, bind it with `->` first and reference the bound identifier — this is BrainCode's sole data-flow channel and keeps argument evaluation order (strictly left-to-right, no side effects) unambiguous.",
