  "nl": "Why does it seem a lot of people are extremely right-wing the last couple of years?",
  "trajectory_steps": [
   "user (None, score=None): Why does it seem a lot of people are extremely right-wing the last couple of years?",
   "model (tiiuae/falcon-7b-instruct, score=78): People may become more right-wing due to a variety of reasons, including changes in the economy, fear of terrorism, and a general dissatisfaction with current political and social systems. In some cases, people may become more extreme due to personal experience or trauma. It's also possible that social media and the internet have increased the visibility of extreme right-wing views, making it easier for people to connect and be influenced. Ultimately, it's important to note that not all people are extreme right-wing, and it's not fair to paint them all with the same brush.\nThere are likely a variety of contributing factors to the current trend of increasing extreme right-wing attitudes, including changes in the economy, fear of terrorism, and dissatisfaction with current political and social systems. Additionally, the rise of social media and the internet may have made it easier for people to connect and be influenced by extreme right-wing viewpoints. It is crucial to recognize that not all individuals with these views are identical",
   "model (claude-instant-1, score=87): There are a few factors that may have contributed. Economic anxieties following the recession pushed some towards more nationalist positions. The rise of populist leaders espousing anti-immigration, traditional values has energized supporters. Changing demographics and social liberalization on issues like marriage equality and gender roles concerns cultural conservatives. The polarizing 2016 election and subsequent political events further galvanized those on the right of the spectrum.",
   "model (google/flan-t5-xxl, score=10): people have gotten more xenophobic",
   "model (claude-2.1, score=74): In the past few years, some factors that may have contributed to more extreme right-wing views gaining traction include:\n\n- Economic anxiety and dissatisfaction with the status quo\n- Reactions against progressive social/cultural changes\n- The rise of partisan media echo chambers and social media algorithms that can reinforce extreme views\n- Politicians using divisive rhetoric to energize their base",
   "user (None, score=None): I understand in for example the USA the economic anxieties must be terrible, but even in civilised countries like the Netherlands people vote more right wing, why?",
   "model (claude-instant-1, score=84): There are several possible reasons for increasing support for right-wing parties even in countries less affected by economic hardship. Issues of national identity and immigration tend to galvanize conservative voters. With globalization, there is a perceived loss of control and culture change that right parties address. The refugee crisis heightened fears over borders and security. Social media allows rapid spread of controversial views. Even center-left parties adopting some right stances on these issues leaves room for true populist right options. Younger generations in all countries appear less bound by traditional partisan ties.",
   "model (claude-instant-1, score=91): There are several possible reasons for rising right-wing populism in countries like the Netherlands as well. Cultural issues around topics like immigration and national identity have galvanized some voters. Economic uncertainties from globalization and technological change affect many western nations. The refugee crisis in Europe heightened fears about border control and cultural change. Meanwhile, centrist parties are seen as not adequately addressing concerns, leaving an opening for far-right parties to voice opposition strongly. The transnational nature of these trends suggests anxieties over national sovereignty and social cohesion play a role beyond any single domestic factor.",
   "feedback: This was a good conversation. I don't think anything was missing."
  ]
