ontrol flow and messaging."}, "improvement": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Named steps and explicit bindings could improve execution planning for straightforward operations. The missing operational semantics for selection, loops, conditions, message drafting, revision, and output delivery mean a weaker agent would still have to infer the most consequential parts from opaque strings, so the current basis does not yet reliably improve planning for the sampled tasks."}}, "simulations": [{"item_id": "dev-code-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Given a list of file paths, delete every file older than 30 days unless it's in the 'archive' folder.", "braincode": "TASK DeleteOldFiles(paths):\n    ACTION delete_matching(collection=paths, criterion=\"older than 30 days unless in archive folder\")", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "The actionable predicate, exception, and required per-file iteration remain opaque prose. ITERATION and CONDITIONAL are referenced by TASK but their definitions are not supplied."}, {"item_id": "dev-email-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Draft a reply to my professor asking for a two-day extension on the assignment, and keep it formal.", "braincode": "TASK DraftExtensionReply:\n    ACTION draft_reply(recipient=\"my professor\", request=\"two-day extension on the assignment\", register=\"formal\") -> draft", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Generic ACTION can carry recipient, request, and register as arbitrary attributes, but no complete ACTION ontology or MESSAGE semantics defines drafting or delivery."}, {"item_id": "b7082615-e6e1-4981-b51b-9259671d1adf", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "Change your store to the one nearest to 07055", "braincode": "TASK ChangeStore:\n    ACTION change_store(zip=\"07055\", selection=\"nearest\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The core action can be named, but change_store and nearest selection have no supplied canonical semantics. Different translators would likely choose different arbitrary verbs."}, {"item_id": "e2adf8f1-547d-4671-96c1-4a21a56e135d", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "View the upcoming schedule from Otis St@Summer St to City Point of the transit near South Station for today.", "braincode": "TASK ViewSchedule:\n    ACTION view_schedule(origin=\"Otis St@Summer St\", destination=\"City Point\", near=\"South Station\", date=\"today\", timing=\"upcoming\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "A generic action records the request fields, but route lookup, station selection, and schedule-view behavior are not defined by the incomplete ontology."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190908_120422_949453#2", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "Move a red rag into a sink.", "braincode": "TASK MoveRag:\n    ACTION move(object=\"red rag\", destination=\"sink\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The simple goal is structurally represented, but move is not among the visible completed canonical definitions and no operational object/location semantics are supplied."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190906_165121_524545#3", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "Put a box with keys in it on a chair.", "braincode": "TASK PutBoxOnChair:\n    ACTION place(object=\"box with keys in it\", destination=\"chair\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The final placement is represented, but containment verification and the implied prerequisite of putting keys in the box are not formally decomposed."}, {"item_id": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-7757", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "The default value for positional only argument has vanished. Reproduce with '.. py:function:: foo(a, b=0, /, c=1)' and restore display of the default value in Sphinx.", "braincode": "TASK FixSphinxDefaultDisplay:\n    ACTION modify_file(path=\"sphinx/util/inspect.py\", goal=\"restore positional-only argument default values in generated signatures\", reproduction=\".. py:function:: foo(a, b=0, /, c=1)\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The coding goal, file, and reproduction are retained only as opaque strings. No code-edit, test, verification, or expected-output constructs are defined."}, {"item_id": "django__django-15268", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "Optimize multiple AlterFooTogether operations into one.", "braincode": "TASK OptimizeAlterFooTogether:\n    ACTION modify_file(path=\"django/db/migrations/operations/models.py\", goal=\"coalesce paired removal and addition AlterUniqueTogether and AlterIndexTogether operations into final operations\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The target and objective survive, but the transformation conditions and expected migration sequence remain natural-language payload."}, {"item_id": "c7033", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "What is an objectively stronger video game, Marvel's Spider-Man 2 or Baldur's Gate 3? But you must pick one.", "braincode": "TASK AnswerGameComparison:\n    ACTION answer(prompt=\"Compare Marvel's Spider-Man 2 and Baldur's Gate 3 by agreed strengths and weaknesses; choose one objectively stronger game\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The answer request and forced-choice constraint are carried as prose. MESSAGE's turn and continuation mechanism was claimed in the overview but not supplied."}, {"item_id": "c1182", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "How to approach a girl; give realistic pickup lines that would work in real life, and be more creative and reliable than generic Google-like answers.", "braincode": "TASK GiveApproachAdvice:\n    ACTION answer(prompt=\"Give creative, realistic, respectful pickup-line and approach advice; avoid generic Google-like answers\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "This is appropriately an open prose payload, but the requested revision/feedback relation and style constraint have no formal MESSAGE representation in the submitted basis."}, {"item_id": "c224", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "Why does it seem a lot of people are extremely right-wing the last couple of years, including in the Netherlands?", "braincode": "TASK ExplainPoliticalTrend:\n    ACTION answer(prompt=\"Explain possible reasons for recent growth in right-w